{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse serde::{Serialize, de::DeserializeOwned};\nuse habeas_sdk::graph::{NodePath, Record};\n\n/// A directory of JSON records. Send + Sync; load/store futures are Send.\n/// Defined in habeas_sdk::storage.\npub struct FileEvidenceStorage { /* private fields */ }\n\npub enum FileStorageError {\n    Io(std::io::Error),\n    Json(serde_json::Error),\n}\n\nimpl FileEvidenceStorage {\n    /// Retain the root directory without performing filesystem I/O.\n    pub fn new(root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self;\n\n    /// Deserialize a record, or return None if its file is missing.\n    pub async fn load<N, M, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n    ) -> Result<Option<Record<N, M, L>>, FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: DeserializeOwned + Send,\n        L: DeserializeOwned + Send,\n        M: DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    /// Atomically replace the record at this node path.\n    pub async fn store<N, M, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        record: &Record<N, M, L>,\n    ) -> Result<(), FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: Serialize + Sync,\n        L: Serialize + Sync,\n        M: Serialize + Sync;\n}\n```\n\n`Record`, `Dependency`, `Fingerprint`, and `Judgment` support Serde\nserialization and deserialization when their type parameters do. These bounds\nbelong to storage use; `Graph` and `EvidenceStorage` themselves do not require them.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in the `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface` text.\n\n- **`new` retains the root without I/O.**\n  - In `storage.rs#fn[paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects]`, the store is built on a non-existent root and `assert!(!root.exists())` holds after construction and the loads.\n  - `storage.rs#fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` also asserts `!root.exists()` after `new` and before the first `store`.\n- **`load` returns `Ok(None)` for a missing record.** The same missing-root test asserts `is_none()` for several path shapes.\n- **`load` returns the deserialized record.**\n  - `storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` stores a record and loads it back. It asserts equality of `procedure`, `dependencies` and `output`.\n  - The test `record` helper uses both `Dependency` variants, `Node` and `OutgoingEdges`, with `Fingerprint`, `Judgment` and JSON metadata.\n  - A second round trip uses a `String` label type for `L`.\n- **`FileStorageError::Json` and `FileStorageError::Io` variants.**\n  - The round-trip test checks the `Json` variant for a type-incompatible load (`u8` for `N`, and `u8` for `L`) and for malformed JSON.\n  - It checks the `Io` variant by making the record path a directory.\n  - It asserts that `to_string` equals the wrapped cause's text.\n  - The nested-path test checks that an over-long key gives `Io` on both load and store.\n  - `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` checks the `Json` error through the `EvidenceStorage` delegation.\n- **`store` atomically replaces the record.** `concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes` runs competing writers against a reader. Every read is a complete record (id \"A\" or \"B\", padding length 8192), and only one entry remains in the directory.\n- **`Send + Sync` and `Send` futures.**\n  - The concurrent test shares `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` across scoped threads, which compiles only if the struct is `Send + Sync`.\n  - The `send(...)` helper wraps both the `store` and `load` futures in the nested-path test, and the `store` and `load_evidence` futures in `contracts.rs#fn[checker_needs_no_validation_and_storage_preserves_nonserializable_metadata]`. This checks `Send` at compile time.\n- **Serde bounds belong to storage use only.** The contracts test stores and loads evidence through a `GraphOnly` graph whose metadata is non-serializable, and the `Checker` runs on it. This shows `Graph` and `EvidenceStorage` need no Serde bounds. Serde support for `Record`, `Dependency`, `Fingerprint` and `Judgment` is exercised by the round trips above.\n\nI found no obligation without an assertion, and no acknowledged or unacknowledged gaps. All the tests carry `{test}` references to the subject.",
  "references": "6de22a4662b3b56e1ca0c5c967c7bc2bffab534cc735b328c21e2f366f729613",
